MID_SE_Die_Nin_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Die_Nin_C_001: ♪
MID_SE_Die_Nin_C_002: Oh...
MID_SE_Die_Nin_C_003: What do you want? Whatever you have to say,\nsay it already.
MID_SE_Die_Nin_C_004: The spirits called me here. Now I see you here,\nin the place where I was called to be.
MID_SE_Die_Nin_C_005: Was that a flute? It sounded a cryptic tone.
MID_SE_Die_Nin_C_006: It's a Har Hali flute. You've probably never seen\none before.
MID_SE_Die_Nin_C_007: The spirits find this sound moving. They told me so.
MID_SE_Die_Nin_C_008: Who? Hey, are you listening to me?
MID_SE_Die_Nin_C_009: They hum with sorrow. Your sorrow. You are a\nwretched, wretched thing.
MID_SE_Die_Nin_C_010: Sorrow? If you're trying to read my mind, you're\nnot very good at it.
MID_SE_Die_Nin_C_011: Being at Orchel's side makes me happy, not sad.\nThere's no reason to pity me.
MID_SE_Die_Nin_C_012: Pity? You are pitiable as I am pitiable.
MID_SE_Die_Nin_C_013: What, so because we're both loners, we're both\n"wretched things"?
MID_SE_Die_Nin_C_014: Not only us. Lead Priest Orchel is also pitiable.\nThat is why I safeguard her.
MID_SE_Die_Nin_C_015: Nothing you say makes sense.
MID_SE_Die_Nin_C_016: Will you not sound your flute again today?
MID_SE_Die_Nin_C_017: Hmph. Think I'm done with that for now.
MID_SE_Die_Nin_C_018: Besides, I don't play this thing for fun. Don't expect\na performance out of me.
MID_SE_Die_Nin_C_019: You play despite dissatisfaction with the playing?\nHow odd you are.
MID_SE_Die_Nin_C_020: I will be elsewhere. To be here longer will only\nprolong your sorrow.
MID_SE_Die_Nin_C_021: If I'm "odd," what does that make her?
MID_SE_Die_Nin_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Die_Nin_B_001: ♪
MID_SE_Die_Nin_B_002: Ahh...
MID_SE_Die_Nin_B_003: Don't clap. I didn't want an audience.
MID_SE_Die_Nin_B_004: Not for my ears, then. Then whose hearing do you\nhope for? Lead Priest Orchel's?
MID_SE_Die_Nin_B_005: Augh... This is just my way of killing time while I\nwait for her.
MID_SE_Die_Nin_B_006: Hm? Why this need for waiting?
MID_SE_Die_Nin_B_007: Even I can't be with Orchel all the time.
MID_SE_Die_Nin_B_008: Sometimes she attends to Credna. Or takes part in\na ceremony just for priests.
MID_SE_Die_Nin_B_009: Besides, I don't want to be in her way now that she's\ngetting to know the outside world.
MID_SE_Die_Nin_B_010: Your aloneness is for Lead Priest Orchel's sake?
MID_SE_Die_Nin_B_011: She wants to give me my space too. Probably thinks\nthat's what I want.
MID_SE_Die_Nin_B_012: She disappeared into the darkness. There went my\nreason to live.
MID_SE_Die_Nin_B_013: Without Orchel, I have nothing. But Credna says we\nshould have faith and wait, so I do.
MID_SE_Die_Nin_B_014: He's trying everything he can to bring her back.
MID_SE_Die_Nin_B_015: But I don't know what to do without her. Except play\nthis flute and wait.
MID_SE_Die_Nin_B_016: The Har Hali flute, which I learned from the people\nwho betrayed me.
MID_SE_Die_Nin_B_017: You dislike your instrument?
MID_SE_Die_Nin_B_018: I don't know. It must have some sentimental value if\nI'm still holding on to it.
MID_SE_Die_Nin_B_019: I like the cry of your flute very much. Its cry is clear\nand sorrowful. My heart cries out this way too.
MID_SE_Die_Nin_B_020: Thanks for the good review.
MID_SE_Die_Nin_B_021: Its tones say more than words. The flute voices\nyour feelings. Your pain. Your sorrow.
MID_SE_Die_Nin_B_022: I hear the real you when it speaks. To hear this\nmakes me glad.
MID_SE_Die_Nin_B_023: Your words are impenetrable. The flute\nbrings clarity.
MID_SE_Die_Nin_B_024: You don't know what you're talking about.\nThe things you say are impenetrable too.
MID_SE_Die_Nin_B_025: Mm? My mouth speaks with my heart's voice.
MID_SE_Die_Nin_B_026: I'd believe that. You don't seem like the type to hide\nanything or fool anyone.
MID_SE_Die_Nin_B_027: Would you play again? I would like to hear your\nplaying. The spirits would like it too.
MID_SE_Die_Nin_B_028: I guess. If you want to listen to my boring flute\nrecitals, I can't stop you.
MID_SE_Die_Nin_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Die_Nin_A_001: Hm? Hey. Hey, Ninae!
MID_SE_Die_Nin_A_002: Diego. Did you call to me?
MID_SE_Die_Nin_A_003: I thought you were here to listen to my flute, but\nthen you walked off.
MID_SE_Die_Nin_A_004: I neither saw nor heard your flute. But I will be\nhappy to hear it when you begin.
MID_SE_Die_Nin_A_005: Hold on. I didn't say I was going to play.
MID_SE_Die_Nin_A_006: No? Did I mishear?
MID_SE_Die_Nin_A_007: Why are you so eager to listen to me play the flute?\nI only do it to kill time.
MID_SE_Die_Nin_A_008: The spirits encouraged me to seek you out. I no\nlonger know why.
MID_SE_Die_Nin_A_009: Do you generally do what the spirits say?
MID_SE_Die_Nin_A_010: No. Theirs is the counsel. Mine is the decision.
MID_SE_Die_Nin_A_011: Open your arms.
MID_SE_Die_Nin_A_012: Huh? You mean like this?
MID_SE_Die_Nin_A_013: Hey, what's the idea? Why are you hugging me?
MID_SE_Die_Nin_A_014: Let it continue. Please. I want to perceive the\nharmony of our souls.
MID_SE_Die_Nin_A_015: U-uh...
MID_SE_Die_Nin_A_016: The sounding of your flute makes my heart feel held.
MID_SE_Die_Nin_A_017: It is a feeling I know from contemplating my mother.\nYou know it too.
MID_SE_Die_Nin_A_018: I remember you saying you could feel my emotions\nfrom the music I played.
MID_SE_Die_Nin_A_019: The melody voiced by a sorrowful soul leaves me\ntrembling. The vibrations carry between our souls.
MID_SE_Die_Nin_A_020: I felt I must feel them with my body. And so I felt\nyours. You're warm and trembling.
MID_SE_Die_Nin_A_021: Yeah, that'll happen when someone hugs you out of\nnowhere. Sheesh.
MID_SE_Die_Nin_A_022: The thudding of your heart was loud enough to\nmake me jump.
MID_SE_Die_Nin_A_023: Any heartbeat is a stranger to me. I found yours to\nbe adorable.
MID_SE_Die_Nin_A_024: And you weren't embarrassed to hug me in broad\ndaylight?
MID_SE_Die_Nin_A_025: Why would I be?
MID_SE_Die_Nin_A_026: Forget I asked. You can be so strange.
MID_SE_Die_Nin_A_027: You are odder than I. You have the power to make\nhearts tremble with an indifferent flute.
MID_SE_Die_Nin_A_028: I'm not that indifferent to it. In fact...well...I've been\npracticing lately.
MID_SE_Die_Nin_A_029: Have you really? Show me. Play for me. I am eager.
MID_SE_Die_Nin_A_030: Alright. Take a seat next to me and I'll get started.